														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-3891364">
									

<p>You have definitely improved this. The interplay between Selks and Everwood really gets her character across, and the conversation with O5-10 especially shows that it's not just a case of the big mean Head Researcher picking on the poor defenseless Level 3. He's a complete shitter, but she's nuanced and unscrupulous in other ways. I can believe now that she would try and promote herself to Administrator.</p>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;That&nbsp;said,&nbsp;found&nbsp;a&nbsp;bunch&nbsp;of&nbsp;typos,&nbsp;all&nbsp;of&nbsp;them&nbsp;in&nbsp;offset&nbsp;3.</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">–&nbsp;hide&nbsp;block</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p>offset 3</p>
<blockquote>
<p>Please place look directly at the screen.</p>
</blockquote>
<blockquote>
<p>the free, wireless power transmission</p>
</blockquote>
<p>don't need 'the'</p>
<blockquote>
<p>Perl Harbor</p>
</blockquote>
<p>I guess this could be intentional?</p>
<blockquote>
<p>and was dismantled</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Missing 'it'.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>merely an inside joke</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Missing 'to'.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>anomalous items; even more so</p>
</blockquote>
<p>That should be a comma.</p>
<p>I don't think it's so much <em>redundancy</em> of amnestics as obsolescence, or just total failure.</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>

