			<div class="content" id="post-content-3899901">
									

<p>Interesting.</p>
<p>I'll say its a slow burn to get to the point where we see the historical connection, but the unraveling of Dr. Selks and the record of altered historical events really intrigued me as a reader. If anything, I would have loved to have seen more reversions of history and the logic behind them, since your presentation here is quite good.</p>
<p>That said, this is not without problems. The way you play the O5s here is a little close to the ground. These are supposed to be the top dogs of the Foundation, and you have them overseeing disputes between Level 3 staff. Shouldn't there be Level 4 Site Directors and such handling this minutia? Additionally, the interview logs between Everwood and 4000 didn't really grab me, as they seemed like the typical &quot;Humanoid skip gets in a researcher's head and causes problem&quot; series of events, and are easily the weakest part of the article for me.</p>
<p>Overall, +1. There are some dings and dents, but through and through a solid contest entry. Well done.</p>

